# === SECRETS — never commit ===
# Credentials, tokens, master passwords. One stray leak burns a public repo.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.token

# OS keyring / cert material
*.key
*.pem
!**/testdata/**/*.pem   # allow synthetic test certs only under testdata/

# === Local vault caches & KeePass files ===
*.kdbx
*.kdbx.lock
*.lock

# The vendored kdbx library ships its own test fixtures — synthetic kdbx files
# and keyfiles from a public MIT repository, with published passwords. Its tests
# cannot run without them, and those tests are what stands between a mistake in
# our KDBX 4.1 patch and silent data loss in a real vault. Scoped to that one
# directory on purpose: the blanket rules above exist so a real vault can never
# be committed by accident, and they stay in force everywhere else.
!third_party/gokeepasslib/tests/**/*.kdbx
!third_party/gokeepasslib/tests/**/*.key

# === PoC / scratch / raw dumps (real data) ===
scratch/
tmp/
*.dump
*.dump.json
dump*.json
offline-package*.json
offlinepackage*.json

# === PoC findings — may hold real data until sanitized ===
FINDINGS.md

# === Real config with credentials ===
config.toml

# === Build / tooling ===
/harmos
/dist/
*.out
coverage.*
.DS_Store
